# An install is a vendored copy compared byte for byte against a tag, so identical content
# must hash identically on every platform. Without this, a clone checked out with
# core.autocrlf=true streams CRLF into `git archive` and every copied file reads as stale:
# measured on one Windows install, where all fourteen blobs differed and all fourteen modes
# matched. Normalize on commit, check out LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz  binary
